<H3>Desktop, server-client, three-tier, cloud or mobile applications</H3>

<p>Whether we're dealing with a simple website, or a complex cloud application, the issues that come up in internationalisation are very often parallel.  Whatever the complexity of your system, and whatever platform it is working on, we can help your technical team prepare it for successful, efficient and high-quality localisation.</p>

<H3>Databases</H3>

<p>One of the most complex tasks we have had to complete in the past has been to prepare often very complex databases to provide multilingual output correctly and consistently.  We can lead you through the logic of this often confusing internationalisation task, all the way from making changes to data structures, query logic and text encoding to inserting translated text data into the internationalised database.</p>

<H3>Single-source authoring</H3>

<p>We have long experience translating from directly inside single-source document management systems, including the hugely successful Author-IT single-source authoring system, ensuring that your business-critical texts are localised centrally (and thus need to be adapted only once).</p>

<H3>Software localisation</H3>

<p>Our ability to help you design workflows using the appropriate tools for your needs is second to none.  We advise you on the right tools to do your localisation work on each development iteration, depending on your needs and goals.</p>

<H3>Encoding</H3>
<p>Many legacy websites and older software architectures use obsolete encoding pages. We recommend using only Unicode (usually UTF8) for all internationalised websites and applications. However, where that is impossible, we can use escape codes to reproduce most Western European scripts.</p>

